{"timestamp":"2026-04-25T15:27:00+08:00","request_id":"req_20260425_151500_qfilters_sw_sanity","stage":"trainer_full_done","next_action":"investigate_harness_bug","actor":"main_inline","status":"BUG_DISCOVERED","notes":"CRITICAL: sliding_window mode PPL=3624.6413031372203, BIT-IDENTICAL to qfilters mode PPL=3624.6413031372203 (same avg_loss 8.195510611534118, same num_tokens 819000). The sanity check reveals: QFiltersAttention.make_forward wraps orig_forward to call cache.compress_layer POST-forward. Per layer.py docstring this 'leaves the current forward unaffected and only shrinks state for subsequent forwards'. But evaluate_ppl creates a fresh cache per chunk and does exactly ONE forward per chunk — compression hook runs but NEVER affects any loss computation. Both modes silently degenerate to full attention, hence identical PPL. Additional bug: data/pg19_chunks.npy has 6441 chunks but vanilla baseline used skip_chunks=40000 (empty slice), making the 5102.22 vs 3624.64 '0.71x' claim apples-to-oranges. Remediation: (1) re-run vanilla at skip_chunks=200 for apples-to-apples; (2) fix eval harness to exercise compression (chunked autoregressive eval where a single long seq is fed as sub-chunks with cache carryover, so compressed state actually feeds attention)."}
